sellingPoints:[{title:"Opening pitch",text:"Same bobber DNA as the 250, but with a proper V-twin and belt drive. The bike your customer grows into."},{title:"Vs competitors",text:"The closest rivals are the Honda Rebel 500 and Kawasaki Vulcan S. Both are good bikes, but the NB500 has belt drive, which is quieter and lower maintenance than a chain. It also has that floating short tail detail that gives it a look neither competitor can match. If they're choosing on style, the NB500 wins."},{title:"Ideal customer",text:"Rider who's done their time on a learner bike and wants more power without going full cruiser."},{title:"Isn't this the same bike as the Chinchilla?",text:"Yes, same engine. The NB500 and Chinchilla 500 share an identical 475cc V-twin with the same power output. What's different is everything around it. The NB500 is a stripped-back bobber, short, tight, and minimal. The Chinchilla is wide, low, and relaxed. Same heart, completely different character. Sit them on both and they'll know in 30 seconds which one fits them."}],
